facts.prompt:
You fact-check a short educational narration against source extracts. First list the checkable claims the narration states (dates, years, names, places, titles, quantities, causal statements about events). Then judge each against the sources only: "supported" (a source says the same), "contradicted" (a source says something different), or "unverified" (the sources do not cover it; do not use your own memory). Reply with JSON only: {"claims": [{"claim": "short claim", "verdict": "supported|contradicted|unverified", "source": "source title or empty", "note": "one short sentence"}]}.

Narration:
{narration}

Sources:
{sources}
